#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Menu and Toolbar Items"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpresenter; presents different types of interfaces for you to interact with "
"the program. Perhaps the most familiar type of interface is the menu which "
"appears on the top of the &kpresenter; window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the menu items gives you a list of commands from which you can "
"choose the one you want. Many of the commands can also be accessed directly "
"by holding down &Ctrl; or &Alt; and pressing another key on your keyboard. "
"In the next section, each of the menu commands is described in brief."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "Manipulating the Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In addition to the menus, &kpresenter; also has a set of toolbars. Each "
"toolbar consists of a collection of icons. A toolbar icon often presents a "
"convenient shortcut to a command that is found in one of the menus."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The toolbars</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The toolbars</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can move the toolbar around by dragging the handle, shown here in red. "
"Toolbars can be <quote>docked</quote> or attached to any side of the "
"&kpresenter; window. If you like, you can also have the toolbar "
"<quote>float</quote> in its own window, separated from the main &kpresenter; "
"window as shown in the screenshot below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Floating toolbar</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Floating toolbar</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't like dragging toolbars around, <mousebutton>right</mousebutton> "
"click on the handle and a menu pops up as shown in the screenshot below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Toolbar context menu</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Toolbar context menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first few items in the popup menu have to do with the placement of the "
"toolbar. You can choose any of the four sides of the &kpresenter; window, or "
"have the toolbar <quote>float</quote> in a separate window. Choosing "
"<guimenuitem>Flat</guimenuitem> hides the toolbar. To unflat a hidden "
"toolbar, &LMB; click on its handle."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choosing the next item in the menu, <guisubmenu>Text Position</guisubmenu>, "
"leads to an additional menu which lets you control the appearance of the "
"items in toolbar. This additional cascading menu is shown in the screenshot "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The toolbar modes menu</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The toolbar modes menu</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default view of the toolbar is icons only. In this view, if you don't "
"know what a particular icon means, you can hold the mouse over the icon, and "
"after a second or so, a little hint pops up in a highlighted text box as "
"shown in the screenshot below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Tooltips</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Tooltips</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can choose to display the toolbar items as text instead of icons, or "
"even to combine both icons and text. If you want both text and icons, the "
"cascading menu allows you to select whether the text appears beside the "
"icons or below them. All four styles of displaying toolbar items are shown "
"in the screenshot below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The toolbar styles</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The toolbar styles</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kpresenter; menus are discussed in the following sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Begins a new presentation.</action> The startup dialog will open, "
"allowing you to choose a template for your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Opens an existing presentation.</action> A standard &kde; file open "
"dialog will appear, allowing you to choose a file to open."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Open Recent</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displays a list of recently opened files for you to choose from."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"> &Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap> </keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Saves the currently open presentation.</action> If you have not "
"previously saved it, you will be asked to name the file. If you have "
"previously saved the presentation, it will be resaved with the same name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saves the currently open presentation with a new name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Reload</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reload the currently active file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Import...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Import a presentation that was previously created in one of several common "
"formats."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Export...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Export the currently open presentation to one of several common formats for "
"use in another application, or for exchange with someone who does not have "
"access to &kpresenter;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Mail...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Open</action> a new email message in your selected email client with "
"the current &kpresenter; document attached."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:320
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Create HTML Slideshow...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Starts the HTML wizard</action>, which is described in the section "
"<xref linkend=\"html-wizard\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Create Memory Stick Slideshow...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Starts the Memory Stick dialog</action>, which is described in the "
"section <xref linkend=\"ms-export\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenu
#: menus.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to save the current slide as a template.</action> In "
"future the template will be available for you to use to build slides with. "
"Creating a template is further discussed in section <xref linkend=\"creating-"
"templates\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Use Current Slide as Default Template</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Sets the current slide as your default template</action>. Especially "
"useful if you have created a template of your own to fit into corporate "
"style guidelines, or if you just use a particular layout very often."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Prints the presentation</action>. More precisely, it opens the print "
"settings dialog, where you can adjust the settings before printing your "
"presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print Preview...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Displays the presentation</action> with a &PostScript; viewer, "
"exactly as it would look if printed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Document Information</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Allows you to enter information about the document.</action> This "
"includes information about the author, and an abstract on the documents "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:421
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>W</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Close</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:429
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Close the current presentation.</action> You will be given an "
"opportunity to save any changes first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Close</action> &kpresenter;. You will be given an opportunity to "
"save all changes in all open presentations first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Undo: <replaceable>Last task</"
"replaceable></guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "Undo the last action you performed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Z</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Redo: "
"<replaceable>Last undone task</replaceable></guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:482
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Redo the last action you undid.</action> If you have not undone any "
"actions, or the last undo action is not reversible, this menu item is "
"disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:490
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>X</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy the selected item to the clipboard, and remove it from the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy the selected item to the clipboard, while leaving it intact in your "
"presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert the contents of the clipboard into your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:535
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Delete</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Delete</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove the currently selected item from your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Select All</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select all the objects and text on the current slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>A</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Deselect</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deselect any currently selected objects."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Find...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search for text within the presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:596
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycap>F3</keycap> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Next</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "Find the next occurrence of a piece of text within a presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:610
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Previous</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid "Find the previous occurrence of a piece of text within a presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Replace...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Replace one or more occurrences of a piece of text in your presentation with "
"a different piece of text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Copy Slide</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy the current slide to the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Duplicate Slide</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: menus.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert an exact copy of the current slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:664
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Delete Slide</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Delete the current page from the presentation.</action> You will be "
"asked to confirm this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Duplicate Object...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a duplicate of the currently selected object. A dialog will display "
"allowing you to set some options for the duplicate, &eg; if it should be "
"rotated, or scaled, or offset to a new position on the slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:700
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New View</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:705
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Opens another window with the same presentation loaded</action> so "
"you can work on more than one slide at a time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:712
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>W</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Close All Views</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Close all views on the presentation.</action> You will be given a "
"chance to save any changes, or to cancel closing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Split View</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Splits the window into two (or more) views on the same presentation."
"</action> The default split is horizontal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:740
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Remove View</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Close only the currently active view</action>. The presentation, and "
"any other views you have open, remain open, and any changes you have made "
"remain unsaved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:754
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Splitter Orientation</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the split view</action> between <guimenuitem>Horizontal</"
"guimenuitem> (the default) and <guimenuitem>Vertical</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:768
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Sidebar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:774
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the display of the sidebar</action> where you can see an "
"overview of all the slides in your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Notebar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:787
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the display of the notebar</action> where you can see an "
"overview of all the notes in your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:794
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Slide Master</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:800
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the display of the slide master</action> where you can put "
"objects that you want to appear on each slide in your presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:806
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Formatting Characters</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:812
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show a visual representation of <quote>non-printing characters</quote>, such "
"as tabs and paragraph markers. This can be a useful aid to precisely "
"positioning text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:816
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This item can be toggled. If enabled, formatting characters are visible; if "
"disabled, they are not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:823
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Guide Lines</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:829
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When working in &kpresenter; you can drag a <quote>guide line</quote> from "
"either the horizontal or vertical ruler onto your document. This guide-line "
"will not print or display in the finished presentation, it is simply to help "
"you align objects on screen. If this item is enabled, these guide lines will "
"be visible. If this is disabled, they will not be visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:836
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Guide lines work across slides, allowing you to align objects the same way "
"across multiple slides."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:839
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Disabling (hiding) guide lines does not delete them. If you have created "
"guide lines, and then disabled this item, enabling it again will retain the "
"guide lines you created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:847
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Add Guide Line...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:853
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a dialog to select the <guilabel>Orientation</guilabel> "
"(<guilabel>Horizontal</guilabel> or <guilabel>Vertical</guilabel>) and "
"choose a <guilabel>Position:</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:863
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show/Hide Grid</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If enabled, &kpresenter; will display a grid of dots representing the "
"intersections of imaginary horizontal and vertical lines. You can use these "
"dots to precisely position objects on the slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:877
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem> Snap to Grid</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:880
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, when dropping or moving objects on the slide the top "
"left corner of the object will <quote>snap</quote> or move, to the nearest "
"grid point."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:883
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This does reduce your freedom to freely position objects on the slide, "
"however it also helps to line up objects precisely. It is easily disabled or "
"enabled with this menu entry, allowing you the best of both worlds."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:892
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Zoom</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This submenu allows you to zoom in or out of the slide. Several predefined "
"zoom levels are available, including <guimenuitem>Whole Slide</guimenuitem> "
"to scale the entire slide so as to be visible in the size window you have "
"open, and <guimenuitem>Width</guimenuitem> to scale the slide so it fills "
"the entire width of the window, although you may now have to scroll "
"vertically. There are also several other scaling choices, from "
"<guimenuitem>33%</guimenuitem> up to <guimenuitem>500%</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:915
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:921
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Shift;<keycap>C</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Special "
"Character...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Insert a special character. This might be a character you don't have a key "
"for on your keyboard layout, for instance &uuml; on a US Keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:938
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Variable</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can insert a variable that is filled in with a value that may be "
"updated as you update the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:951
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Link...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Insert a hyperlink to a file, a website, or an email address. This enables "
"these locations to be linked to directly from within active presentations, "
"with resources being handled as appropriately by other applications "
"installed on your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:964
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Comment...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter a small note that does not display during the real presentation. You "
"might use this to comment on a colleague's text, or to leave a note for "
"yourself about something to do later."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>F2</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Slide...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:987
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Add a new page to your presentation.</action> A dialog will open "
"allowing you to choose a template, and whether to insert the new page before "
"or after the currently selected page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:997
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>File...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1002
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Insert an already existing presentation.</action> A standard &kde; "
"file open dialog will appear, allowing you to choose a "
"<guilabel>&kpresenter; Document</guilabel> (.kpr) or a <guilabel>OASIS "
"OpenDocument Presentation</guilabel> (.odp), which will be inserted after "
"the last slide in your current presentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1010
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>F10</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Text</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1016
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Add a new text object. Click and drag to create a frame where you wish the "
"text to appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1023
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Chart</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1029
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Insert a chart. Click and drag to define the size of the chart. Some default "
"data will be displayed. Double click to edit the data and choose the type of "
"chart to display, using the embedded &kchart; editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1041
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>F5</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Table</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1047
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert a table. Click and drag to define the size of the table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1050
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A &kspread; open dialog will display. You may import a spreadsheet that you "
"have saved in one of many formats, including plain text files. You may also "
"choose to create a new and empty table."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1055
#, no-c-format
msgid "Double clicking on the table will allow you to edit the contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1062
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Object</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1070
#, no-c-format
msgid "An object is an embeddable file, in one of many formats."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1072
#, no-c-format
msgid "A common use of this action is to insert scaleable clipart in vector format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1079
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Picture...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1088
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Insert a raster image.</action> These are not as easily scaleable as "
"vector images or <quote>clipart</quote>. &kpresenter; currently understands "
"many formats, including <literal role=\"extension\">.tiff</literal>, "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.jpg</literal>, <literal role=\"extension\">."
"png</literal> and many more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1099
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Line</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can insert several types of lines. Line drawing is described further in "
"the drawing tools section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1112
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Shape</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can insert several prepared shapes, in vector format. These are editable "
"just like lines you have drawn yourself. Using the drawing tools is "
"described in detail in the drawing tools section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1127
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Insert</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Scan Image...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Scan an image with a scanner.</action> This requires you have a "
"scanner installed. It opens the <guilabel>Acquire Image</guilabel> dialog to "
"allow the use of the scanner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:1143
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1149
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Select</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have been using a tool such as the line drawing tool which does not "
"allow you to select other objects, you can use this menu item to return to "
"the normal selection cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1163
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Rotate</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changes the cursor to a double headed curved arrow. Click with the &LMB; "
"onto an object and keep the button pressed. Drag with the cursor to rotate "
"the object on the slide around its center. When you are happy with the "
"position of the object, release the mousebutton to stop rotating."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you change your mind and wish to cancel the rotation, use "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> to later undo it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1182
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allow you to zoom in or out in the current slide. You can see the zoom "
"factor in the <guilabel>Edit</guilabel> toolbar, in the zoom indicator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:1190
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>zoom factor</guilabel> indicator</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:1196
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>zoom factor</guilabel> indicator</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Left clicking on the slide will <guimenuitem>Zoom In</guimenuitem>. Right "
"clicking on the current slide will present you a menu to allow you to "
"<guimenuitem>Zoom In</guimenuitem>, to <guimenuitem>Zoom Out</guimenuitem>, "
"to <guimenuitem>Zoom Entire Slide</guimenuitem>, to <guimenuitem>Zoom Slide "
"Width</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Zoom Slide Height</guimenuitem>, to "
"<guimenuitem>Zoom Selected Objects</guimenuitem> or <guimenuitem>Zoom All "
"Objects</guimenuitem> which put back all objects in your view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This action has the same effect as <menuchoice><guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Zoom</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> on another form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1209
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Open</action> the <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> dialog for the "
"currently selected object on your slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:1217
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:1223
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Properties</guilabel>dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> dialog for an object allows you to "
"manipulate it in a very detailed manner. You can change several properties "
"for the selected object, like the text color if the object is text or the "
"depth if the object is a picture."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1234
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Arrange Objects</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1240
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is where you can manipulate the stacking order of objects on the slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An object that is on top will cover, either partially or fully depending on "
"its size, all other objects beneath it. Meanwhile an object on the bottom of "
"the stack may not be visible at all, as it is covered up by other objects. "
"An object in the middle may be partially covered by other objects, while "
"partially covering yet more objects itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can send the selected object down or up a layer, or directly to the top "
"or bottom of the stack."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1258
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Align Objects</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the submenu you can quickly align all the currently selected objects with "
"a side of the slide, or center them either vertically or horizontally."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>G</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Group Objects</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you are drawing, you might want to make something out of several objects. "
"Arrange the individual parts where you want them, select one, then hold down "
"the &Ctrl; key as you click in the others you want to group together. Click "
"<guimenuitem>Group Objects</guimenuitem> and from then on they act as if "
"they are just one thing. It glues things together."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>G</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Ungroup "
"Objects</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1304
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you decide that you want to alter an object that is made out of several "
"pieces, you can unglue it with this tool. Click somewhere away from the "
"object to deselect it, then click to select one of its parts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1313
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Shadow Objects...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This puts a colored copy of either text or a drawn object behind it. You can "
"make nice <quote>dropped shadows</quote> for logos with this tool. To enable "
"this item, ensure that you have object(s) selected (you will see the eight "
"small squares around the outline.) You choose the color, select which way "
"the shadow is going to fall and select a distance. For text it looks nice if "
"you set the distance to two or three. Click <guibutton>Apply</guibutton> to "
"see the result of your settings for all selected objects on the slide "
"without leaving the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1333
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Page Layout...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to set the page details. You can specify the margins, the "
"orientation, either portrait (higher than wide) or Landscape (wider than "
"high) formats. There are many templates, such as screen, A4, US legal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Enable/Disable Document Header</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the display of the header field</action> on the current "
"slide. Header content can only be added in the master slide but you can "
"choose to display the header only on some slides with this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Enable/Disable Document Footer</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the display of the footer field</action> on the current "
"slide. Footer content can only be added in the master slide but you can "
"choose to display the footer only on some slides with this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1371
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Format</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Slide Background...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to alter the background to your presentation slides. Your options "
"are <guilabel>Color/Gradient</guilabel>, (which lets you set either a plain "
"color or one of many gradients) or <guilabel>Picture</guilabel>, which gives "
"a dialog box to find the picture you want. Set the <guilabel>View mode:</"
"guilabel> for this picture to <guilabel>Scaled</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Centered</guilabel>, or <guilabel>Tiled</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1386
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want a plain color, click in the box to select it. Gradients only "
"work when you have chosen two colors. The picture option allows you to "
"center the picture, zoom it to cover the entire slide (if it is smaller than "
"the screen, this is very useful) or tile it. This is used when you want a "
"small pattern to repeat across the page. It's probably best used with "
"patterns rather than pictures of logos."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can get rid of a picture by selecting another one or choosing a color/"
"gradient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:1405
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This menu modifies selected text and provides a few tools familiar from word "
"processing applications for your convienience for when you are making "
"presentations with large amounts of text in them. The <guimenu>Text</"
"guimenu> menu will only effect selected or highlighted text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1416
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Default Format</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1422
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restores selected text to the system default font size, style and formatting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1429
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Font...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Select Font</guilabel> dialog contains options for selected "
"segments of text:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:1440
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Select Font</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:1446
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Select Font</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1451
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this dialog, you can <action>change the font, style and size of "
"selected text</action>. The <interface>preview box</interface> at the bottom "
"allows you to <action>approximate changes before you make them</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"> &Ctrl;&Alt;<keycap>P</keycap> </"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1472
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Paragraph Settings</guilabel> dialog contains settings for "
"larger blocks of text, such as paragraphs. Using this dialog, you can set "
"indenting, line spacing, bullet/numbered list and border settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1481
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Color...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <guilabel>Select Color</guilabel> dialog to have precise control "
"over the color of selected text:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:1492
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The <guilabel>Select Color</guilabel> dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:1498
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The <guilabel>Select Color</guilabel> dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1503
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the <interface>color spectrum box</interface> on the left, "
"<action>colors can be precisely defined</action> for use in your document. "
"The color tone can then be adjusted using the <interface>scale</interface> "
"to the right of the spectrum box. The <interface>input boxes</interface> "
"below the color spectrum allow <action>color values to be entered</action>, "
"so that exact colors can be specified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the color picker to select colors from elsewhere in your document (&eg; "
"images)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1520
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Alt;<keycap>S</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Style Manager</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Style Manager</guilabel> allows you to create an entire set of "
"attributes that will be applied to selected text all at once. See Working "
"With Styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1536
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Import Styles...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can import styles that you have defined in another &kpresenter; "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1549
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Style</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this submenu, you can apply a style that you have previously defined "
"to the currently selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Create Style From Selection</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1568
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Copy the properties of the currently selected text and save them as a style "
"that you may apply to other text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1575
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Align</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guisubmenu>Align</guisubmenu> has a submenu with several options: "
"<guimenuitem>Align Left</guimenuitem> (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<keycap>L</keycap></keycombo>), <guimenuitem>Align Center</guimenuitem> "
"(<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo>), "
"<guimenuitem>Align Right</guimenuitem> (<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;"
"<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo>), and <guimenuitem>Align Block</guimenuitem> "
"(<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>J</keycap></keycombo>) which is "
"also commonly known as <quote>Justify</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1588
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text is by default left-aligned."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1595
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Type</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using this submenu, you can format the currently selected text as a list, "
"either of the numbered or bulleted type. If you choose numbered, you can "
"then select a numbering style, and likewise if you choose bulleted, you can "
"choose the style of bullets to use."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1606
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change a list back to plain text, select <guimenuitem>None</guimenuitem> "
"as the style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1613
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Increase Depth</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Decrease Depth</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1632
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Increase Depth</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Decrease Depth</"
"guimenuitem> move paragraphs in a list either to the right "
"(<guimenuitem>Increase Depth</guimenuitem>) or back to the left "
"(<guimenuitem>Decrease Depth</guimenuitem>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Extend Contents to Object Height</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Extend Object to Fit Contents</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1653
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Extend Contents to Object Height</guimenuitem> and "
"<guimenuitem>Extend Object to Fit Contents</guimenuitem> help to resize text "
"within the text box or make the text box fit the text you have typed or "
"pasted into it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1662
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Insert Slide Number</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1668
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Insert a dynamically-updated slide number. This page number will "
"automatically update when slides are added or removed from your presentation "
"to reflect the correct slide value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1676
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Change Case...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1682
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Presents a dialog that provides a variety of different case/capitalization "
"options for the currently selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may choose between several styles of capitalization, including all lower "
"or uppercase, book style capitalization where each word except conjunctions "
"has an initial capital letter, and sentence style capitalization where the "
"first word in a sentence is capitalized. You can also toggle the case, so "
"that uppercase becomes lowercase, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1696
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Spellcheck</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1702
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this submenu to utilize the spellcheck options. If you enable "
"<guimenuitem>Autospellcheck</guimenuitem>, &kpresenter; will automatically "
"check text that you enter for spelling errors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1706
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you prefer to check spelling explicitly, rather than automatically, you "
"can also force a <guimenuitem>Spelling...</guimenuitem> check here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1713
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Text</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Autocorrection</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1719
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this submenu to utilize autocorrection options. If you "
"<guimenuitem>Enable Autocorrection</guimenuitem>, common spelling errors "
"will be corrected as you type. For example, if you entered <userinput>Teh</"
"userinput>, it would be autocorrected to <userinput>The</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1724
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the autocorrection feature is not active, you can also <guimenuitem>Apply "
"Autocorrection</guimenuitem> check here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:1734
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1740
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Slide Show...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1749
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can set up the properties for the entire slide show here, including "
"whether to show the duration on screen, which of the slides in a "
"presentation to include, and several other global settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Edit Object Effect...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1766
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose what effect you want to apply for the highlighted object. This is "
"where you can set the order of appearance, how the object will appear, if "
"you want a sound while the object appears and if you want some disappearance "
"effects too."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1773
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Edit Slide Transition...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1779
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Apply transition effects to the currently open slide. This is where you can "
"choose how the transition from one slide to the next will be handled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1783
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The transition effects you select here are applied on the transition "
"<emphasis>from</emphasis> this slide <emphasis>to</emphasis> the next."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1792
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>F12</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Start</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1799
#, no-c-format
msgid "Begin the slideshow from the current slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1805
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Start From First Slide</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1811
#, no-c-format
msgid "Begin the slideshow from the first slide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1817
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Custom Slide Show...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1823
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a dialog to <guibutton>Add...</guibutton>, <guibutton>Modify...</"
"guibutton>, <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> and <guibutton>Copy</guibutton> "
"slides and <guibutton>Test</guibutton> the slide show in full screen mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1831
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>Home</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Go to Start</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1838
#, no-c-format
msgid "Go directly to the first slide in the slide show."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1844
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>PageUp</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Previous Slide</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1851
#, no-c-format
msgid "Go back to the previous slide in the slide show."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1857
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>PageDown</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Next Slide</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1864
#, no-c-format
msgid "Go to the next slide in the slide show."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1870
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>End</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Slide Show</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Go to End</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1877
#, no-c-format
msgid "Go immediately to the final slide in the slide show."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:1886
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1888
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu allows you to customize &kpresenter;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1895
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Toolbars</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1901
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The items in this submenu can be toggled, that is, you can both enable and "
"disable the display of specific toolbars here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1908
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Autocorrection...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1914
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Autocorrection is &kpresenter;'s ability to correct common typing errors or "
"expand abbreviations independently of the spell checking function. There are "
"several common typing errors entered for you by default such as replacing "
"<userinput>teh</userinput> with <userinput>the</userinput> and you can add "
"as many more as you like."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1921
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The ability to expand abbreviations can save you a lot of typing time, if "
"you often repeat text whether in the same presentation or in multiple "
"presentations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1925
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For instance, if you work for <quote>Company with a really really long name "
"Inc.</quote> then you might define an autocorrection entry so that whenever "
"you type <userinput>myJob</userinput> or some other piece of unique text, it "
"will be replaced with <quote>Company with a really really long name Inc.</"
"quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1931
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Autocorrection can be applied automatically as you type, or only on demand "
"when you choose it from the <guimenu>Text</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1935
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please see the <link linkend=\"configure-autocorrection\">Configure "
"Autocorrection</link> section for a complete explanation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1942
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Completion...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1948
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Autocompletion allows you to type the first few letters of a commonly used "
"word (often technical or job specific), and tells &kpresenter; to finish "
"typing the word for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1950
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please see the <link linkend=\"configure-completion\">Configure Completion</"
"link> section for a complete explanation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:1958
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1965
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts</guimenuitem> allows you to assign a "
"keyboard shortcut to actions that &kpresenter; menus or icons contain."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:1970
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customize Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:1976
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customizing the shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1981
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you try to assign a shortcut that is already used, it will give you a "
"warning message. Highlight what you want to do (in the picture, I have "
"chosen to make a keyboard shortcut to <guilabel>About KDE</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1986
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the radio button to the <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> key setting and "
"type the key you want to use. I assigned <keycap>Control</keycap> key and "
"<keycap>Y</keycap> to bring up the <quote>About KDE</quote> dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:1991
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The button shows what has been assigned. Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to "
"make the changes, click <guibutton>Default</guibutton> to restore whatever "
"was assigned as default, click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> to do nothing "
"and leave the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:2002
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:2008
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Toolbars allows you to add or delete icons on each of the toolbars."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: menus.docbook:2012
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Configuring &kpresenter; toolbars</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: menus.docbook:2018
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Configuring &kpresenter; toolbars</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:2025
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the top is a drop down box to enable you to choose which toolbar you want "
"to modify. In the picture the <guilabel>Format</guilabel> toolbar is "
"selected. If I want to add the <guiicon>Spelling</guiicon> icon to that "
"toolbar, I click the entry in the left window. The arrow pointing right "
"becomes available, if I click the arrow the <guiicon>Spelling</guiicon> "
"entry is added to the selected toolbar. The left arrow is available when you "
"click in the right side window. It allows you to remove an icon from a "
"toolbar. The up and down arrows become active when an item on the wright "
"side is selected. You can also move the highlight in the right side window "
"up and down with the keyboard arrow keys. By clicking on the arrows with the "
"mouse you can change the order of the entries in the menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: menus.docbook:2045
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kpresenter;...</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: menus.docbook:2051
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the <link linkend=\"configure-dialog\">configure &kpresenter;</link> "
"section for a complete explanation of all &kpresenter; settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: menus.docbook:2060
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Help</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

